  "body": "The turning insert model is the nose circle only: insert shape, approach (lead) angle, clearance and a sharp nose aren't modelled.\n\n**Where:** the `Turning` kind reads only `nose_radius`, and `is_sane` requires `nose_radius > 0` (`crates/tools/src/tools.rs:268`).\n\n**Effect:**\n- A 35° V insert and an 80° C insert of the same nose radius are the same tool to CamCraft. So are a 93° and a 72.5° neutral holder.\n- A sharp-nose insert (0 radius, used for fine finishing and small diameters) is refused outright.\n- Flank clearance isn't judged. *Guess:* back-turning or profiling a shoulder with a narrow-angle insert could rub the trailing flank unseen.\n\n**Fix sketch:** model the insert from its ISO 1832 designation (a public standard): shape and included angle, clearance, IC and nose radius; plus the holder's approach angle and hand. Judge the full insert outline in the turning envelope and gouge laws. Allow a sharp nose with an explicit minimum.\n\nEffort: max (geometry plus the collision laws).\n\n**Done means:** an insert's outline (not just its nose circle) is swept by the turning verdicts; a profile the insert's flank can't reach is refused by name; pinned.\n",
